// Tessera stdlib: what the correctly rounded sin_pi, cos_pi and tan_pi of F64 share
//
// sin(pi s/2048) and cos(pi s/2048) for an angle index s, from tables of sin(pi i/64) and of sin and cos of
// pi j/2048 (to about 2^-75, and to double-double accuracy for the accurate phase), the double-double helpers,
// and the accurate phase sin_pi and cos_pi both end in.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/sinpi/sinpi.c and src/binary64/cospi/cospi.c via RazorForge's B64TrigPi.rf
// (the helpers and tables appear identically in both files, and tanpi.c repeats the double-double helpers).
// Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

